= Solution
{parent=i}

Use base-two <logarithms>, so <entanglement entropy> is measured in bits. Write $h_2(p)=-p\log_2p-(1-p)\log_2(1-p)$ for the <binary entropy>, with $0\log_20=0$. Taking a <partial trace> over any two parties removes the off-diagonal terms: the two traced strings are orthogonal. Consequently all three one-party <reduced density matrices> of the first <pure state> are
$$
\rho_A=\rho_B=\rho_C=p|0\rangle\langle0|+(1-p)|1\rangle\langle1|.
$$
Each division into two groups is one party versus the other two. The <Schmidt coefficients> are $\sqrt p$ and $\sqrt{1-p}$, so **the entanglement entropy across each of $A:BC$, $B:AC$ and $C:AB$ is $h_2(p)$**. For the second <pure state>, set $p=1/2$: every one-party <reduced density matrix> is $I/2$, and **all three entanglement entropies are one bit**.

For every pair $XY$, the first <pure state> instead gives the <reduced density matrix>
$$
\rho_{XY}=p|00\rangle\langle00|+(1-p)|11\rangle\langle11|.
$$
This is a <separable quantum state>, explicitly a <convex combination> of two <product states>. Its <relative entropy of entanglement> is therefore zero: in $E_R(\rho)=\inf_{\sigma\in\mathrm{Sep}}D(\rho\|\sigma)$, choose $\sigma=\rho$ to attain zero, while <nonnegativity of quantum relative entropy> excludes a negative value. The same argument with equal weights applies to the second <pure state>. Thus
$$
\boxed{E_R(\rho_{AB})=E_R(\rho_{AC})=E_R(\rho_{BC})=0\quad\text{for both states}.}
$$
The pairwise <density matrices> contain classical correlations, despite the <entanglement> of the global <pure state>; discarding a party loses the coherence between its two branches.

The <entanglement entropy> of $n$ independent source copies across any cut is $nh_2(p)$, whereas $f(n)$ copies of the target <GHZ state> have <entanglement entropy> $f(n)$. <Average monotonicity of pure-state entanglement entropy> under <LOCC> gives $P(n)f(n)\leq nh_2(p)$ for exact successful forward branches. In a reversible asymptotic conversion the reverse direction similarly prevents a first-order deficit, since $n'/n\to1$. For asymptotically faithful outputs, a <continuity bound for quantum conditional entropy> with trivial conditioning changes these inequalities only by $o(n)$. Hence **the reversible leading-order rate is**
$$
\boxed{f(n)=nh_2(p)+o(n),\qquad \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{f(n)}n=h_2(p).}
$$
The zero pairwise <relative entropies of entanglement> are consistent with this conversion: no independent pairwise resource has to be supplied or removed.

There is a qualification to the literal finite-block formulation in the source. For $0<p<1$, the <Schmidt rank> of the exact state of $n'$ source copies is $2^{n'}$, whereas $f$ target <GHZ states> have <Schmidt rank> $2^f$. Every refined <LOCC> branch acts by a product of local <linear operators> and cannot increase this <Schmidt rank>. For $p\ne1/2$, the displayed rate has $f<n'$ for sufficiently large blocks when $n'/n\to1$, so an exact successful reverse conversion is impossible, irrespective of its claimed probability. The <exact dilution obstruction from Schmidt rank> is avoided in the usual asymptotic formulation by allowing outputs approaching the desired <pure state>. The leading-order rate above and the exact forward protocol below remain valid; neither establishes the source's stronger exact round-trip claim. At $p=1/2$ the two states are identical. At $p=0$ or $1$, the source is a known <product state>, the rate is zero, and local preparation supplies any desired number of source copies.

= ii
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

Here is a <tripartite Schmidt projection entanglement concentration> protocol. For $0<p<1$, set $q=1-p$. Regrouping the $n$ local <qubits> of each party gives
$$
|\Psi_1\rangle^{\otimes n}=\sum_{x\in\{0,1\}^n}p^{(n-|x|)/2}q^{|x|/2}|x\rangle_A|x\rangle_B|x\rangle_C,
$$
where $|x|$ counts ones. Alice performs a <projective measurement> of that count, without learning the individual string. The <orthogonal projector> for outcome $k$ is $\Pi_k=\sum_{|x|=k}|x\rangle\langle x|$. By the <Born rule>, its <probability> and conditional <pure state> are
$$
P_k=\binom nk p^{n-k}q^k,\qquad
|T_k\rangle=\frac1{\sqrt{d_k}}\sum_{|x|=k}|x\rangle_A|x\rangle_B|x\rangle_C,\qquad d_k=\binom nk.
$$
Alice sends $k$ by <classical communication>; all three parties use <local unitary operations> to relabel the same ordered type class as $0,\ldots,d_k-1$. There are now $d_k$ equal common-label amplitudes. Measuring the individual <qubits> instead would have destroyed precisely this coherence.

To obtain an integer number $f$ of target <GHZ states>, choose $m=2^f\leq d_k$. The following exact <LOCC> step handles type classes whose sizes are not powers of two. For every $m$-element subset $S\subseteq\{0,\ldots,d_k-1\}$, Alice uses the <Kraus operator>
$$
K_S=\frac{\Pi_S}{\sqrt{\binom{d_k-1}{m-1}}},\qquad \Pi_S=\sum_{r\in S}|r\rangle\langle r|.
$$
Every label occurs in $\binom{d_k-1}{m-1}$ such subsets, proving $\sum_SK_S^\dagger K_S=I$ on the occupied subspace. Thus this is a complete <quantum measurement>. Each outcome has <probability> $m/[d_k\binom{d_k-1}{m-1}]=1/\binom{d_k}{m}$, and leaves the normalized <pure state> $m^{-1/2}\sum_{r\in S}|r,r,r\rangle$. After Alice communicates $S$, all parties relabel its elements in the same order. Binary expansion of the labels then factors the state into **exactly $f$ independent copies of the target GHZ state**. Local extensions of these operations handle unused basis vectors and do not affect the protocol.

For example, taking $f(k)=\lfloor\log_2d_k\rfloor$ gives an outcome-dependent yield without any failure branch. Since $K$ has a <binomial distribution> with parameters $(n,q)$, the <weak law of large numbers> gives $K/n\to q$ in probability. <Stirling's formula>, uniformly when $k/n$ stays away from zero and one, gives
$$
\log_2\binom nk=nh_2(k/n)-\frac12\log_2\bigl(2\pi n(k/n)(1-k/n)\bigr)+O(n^{-1}).
$$
By continuity of the <binary entropy>, $f(K)/n\to h_2(q)=h_2(p)$ in probability. The integer rounding and logarithmic correction have no first-order effect.

A fixed yield with success probability tending to one is also explicit. For sufficiently large $n$, take
$$
f_n=\left\lfloor nh_2(p)-n^{3/4}\right\rfloor.
$$
On $|K-nq|\leq n^{2/3}$, the bounded derivative of the <binary entropy> in a neighborhood of the fixed $q\in(0,1)$ and <Stirling's formula> give $\log_2d_K\geq nh_2(q)-C_qn^{2/3}-O(\log n)\geq f_n$. <Chebyshev's inequality> bounds the complementary <probability> by $q(1-q)n^{-1/3}$. Abort there if necessary, and otherwise use the subset <quantum measurement> with $m=2^{f_n}$. Thus
$$
\boxed{P(\text{success})\longrightarrow1,\qquad f_n/n\longrightarrow h_2(p).}
$$
This matches the first-order rate in part (i), with exact outputs on every successful forward branch. If $p=1/2$, simply retain the original $n$ target copies; if $p$ is an endpoint, output zero target copies.

